  "details": "When you enter the 'Groups' tab on your profile and you see a display of all the groups you have joined, there's no visual to clue to see what groups have set their visibility to 'hidden' (as in, people that click your profile and go into your groups tab can't see them) you have to go one by one checking which are hidden and which are not.\n\nA crossed eye sign at the right corner on top of each one would be enough, where the star is displayed. I think this would be a great UI addition. You could also just divide the groups into tabs, each one for their visibility (public, friends only, hidden).\n\nAlso it would be great if you could set a default visibility status for the groups you join, so maybe you want to set all of the groups you join to be 'hidden' by default.",
